    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493308999/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Thursday, April 27, 1916, I Tatti
Salvemini 
Divine
Walked with B.B. and Salvemini. Geoffrey went down to receive Marcella who had been spending the afternoon with “Mattia”. What a silly girl, acting on the barest sex impulses and talking such long-aided talk about the linea estetica of her inner life, etc. I am getting rather bored with her, though Geoffrey lives on it. 
Ferrando and his tragic lady-love and their Belgian guest, and young painter named Jeanne, came to dine. 
April 28-29 [Pages cut off]"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 108 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1916> .

